# AWS KMS Key Provisioning & File Encryption with Terraform

## Task Overview

Provision a symmetric [AWS KMS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/) key named `devops-kms-key` (with alias `alias/devops-kms-key`), encrypt `/home/bob/terraform/SensitiveData.txt` into base64-encoded ciphertext saved at `/home/bob/terraform/EncryptedData.bin`, decrypt it to verify content parity, and expose `kke_kms_key_name` in `outputs.tf` while maintaining zero state drift in [Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/docs).

## Architecture Flow

```text
+-----------------------+       +----------------------------------+       +-------------------------+
| SensitiveData.txt     | ----> | Terraform (aws_kms_key + alias)  | ----> | AWS KMS (devops-kms-key)|
| (/home/bob/terraform) |       | main.tf & outputs.tf             |       | Key ID: b491807d-...    |
+-----------------------+       +----------------------------------+       +-------------------------+
                                                  |                                      |
                                                  | local-exec (AWS CLI)                 | Encrypt / Decrypt
                                                  v                                      v
                                +----------------------------------+       +-------------------------+
                                | EncryptedData.bin (Base64)       | ----> | DecryptedData.txt       |
                                | diff -s verified (0 changes)     |       | Matches original text   |
                                +----------------------------------+       +-------------------------+
Configuration Files
main.tf
Terraform
resource "aws_kms_key" "devops_kms_key" {
  description             = "Symmetric KMS key for Nautilus DevOps data security"
  deletion_window_in_days = 7
  enable_key_rotation     = true

  tags = {
    Name = "devops-kms-key"
  }
}

resource "aws_kms_alias" "devops_kms_key_alias" {
  name          = "alias/devops-kms-key"
  target_key_id = aws_kms_key.devops_kms_key.key_id
}

resource "null_resource" "kms_encrypt_decrypt" {
  triggers = {
    key_id = aws_kms_key.devops_kms_key.key_id
  }

  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = <<-EOT
      aws kms encrypt \
        --key-id ${aws_kms_key.devops_kms_key.key_id} \
        --plaintext fileb:///home/bob/terraform/SensitiveData.txt \
        --output text \
        --query CiphertextBlob > /home/bob/terraform/EncryptedData.bin

      aws kms decrypt \
        --ciphertext-blob fileb://<(base64 -d /home/bob/terraform/EncryptedData.bin) \
        --output text \
        --query Plaintext | base64 -d > /home/bob/terraform/DecryptedData.txt
    EOT
    interpreter = ["/bin/bash", "-c"]
  }

  depends_on = [aws_kms_alias.devops_kms_key_alias]
}
outputs.tf
Terraform
output "kke_kms_key_name" {
  description = "Name of the KMS key created"
  value       = replace(aws_kms_alias.devops_kms_key_alias.name, "alias/", "")
}
